1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:01,547
Oil helps your carrots.

2
00:00:01,547 --> 00:00:02,823
Heat costs your peppers.

3
00:00:03,623 --> 00:00:04,488
One pan.

4
00:00:04,488 --> 00:00:05,583
Two opposite things

5
00:00:05,583 --> 00:00:07,006
happening to your
veggies.

6
00:00:07,906 --> 00:00:10,195
Bright veggies like
carrots are full of

7
00:00:10,195 --> 00:00:12,281
plant pigments called
carotenoids.

8
00:00:12,281 --> 00:00:14,300
Your body turns them
into vitamin A.

9
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:16,721
Here's the catch.

10
00:00:16,721 --> 00:00:18,163
Those pigments get
absorbed

11
00:00:18,163 --> 00:00:19,451
better with a little
fat.

12
00:00:20,451 --> 00:00:21,757
Think of it like a ride.

13
00:00:21,757 --> 00:00:23,689
The pigments travel
along with the oil.

14
00:00:24,889 --> 00:00:27,094
So a splash of oil isn't
just for flavor.

15
00:00:28,194 --> 00:00:30,554
Same story for vitamins
E and K,

16
00:00:30,554 --> 00:00:32,411
in spinach and broccoli.

17
00:00:32,411 --> 00:00:33,456
Fat helps them in.

18
00:00:34,456 --> 00:00:35,638
Now the flip side.

19
00:00:35,638 --> 00:00:37,989
Peppers, broccoli and
tomatoes are

20
00:00:37,989 --> 00:00:39,467
packed with vitamin C.

21
00:00:40,567 --> 00:00:42,622
Vitamin C dissolves in
water,

22
00:00:42,622 --> 00:00:45,294
and cooking can lower
how much is left.

23
00:00:46,694 --> 00:00:49,342
Microwaving and steaming
can lower it too,

24
00:00:49,342 --> 00:00:50,881
so it's not just the
pan.

25
00:00:51,681 --> 00:00:53,521
That's why raw fruit and
veg

26
00:00:53,521 --> 00:00:55,043
top the vitamin C lists.

27
00:00:55,943 --> 00:00:57,897
So sautéing isn't good
or bad.

28
00:00:57,897 --> 00:00:58,699
It's a trade.

29
00:00:59,999 --> 00:01:01,423
This isn't a diet rule.

30
00:01:01,423 --> 00:01:03,059
It's just what your pan
is doing.

31
00:01:04,559 --> 00:01:06,836
The Pan Theory: carrots
like company.

32
00:01:06,836 --> 00:01:08,524
Tonight, give them a
little oil.

